=== 2D SCREEN BUFFER [80x24] ===
--- TEXT MATRIX ---
00: |   Pigasus CLI Changelog                                                        |
01: |                                                                                |
02: |  The terminal-first surface to interact with Pigasus agents. Stay in your flow |
03: |without context switching.                                                      |
04: |                                                                                |
05: |  ## 1.5.17                                                                     |
06: |                                                                                |
07: |  • Added mouse cursor placement and text selection inside the prompt box in    |
08: |  the full screen (altscreen) rendering mode: click to move the cursor, or      |
09: |  drag and double-click (and double-click-drag by word) to highlight text for   |
10: |  typing or paste replacement, Backspace/Delete, Ctrl+C copy, and Ctrl+X cut    |
11: |  without overwriting your clipboard on release. When Vim mode is on, mouse     |
12: |  selections outside Insert mode enter characterwise Visual mode so Vim         |
13: |  operators and motions act on the selection, and Normal-mode clicks past the   |
14: |  end of a line land on the last character.                                     |
15: |  • Improved background shell command tracking by letting run_command set a     |
16: |  NotificationTimeoutSeconds wakeup, so the CLI automatically notifies the      |
17: |  agent when a long-running command is still running instead of spending extra  |
18: |  turns on separate polling timers.                                             |
19: |  • Improved the Orchestrator row in /model so that picking the same model and  |
20: |  thinking Effort for both Planner and Executor runs single-agent directly on   |
21: |  (0–20 of 4455 lines)                                                          |
22: |                                                                                |
23: |  ↑/↓ Navigate · esc Cancel                                                     |
